    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d376">

                <pb facs="0534" n="410" xml:id="pg410"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.74/62: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-02-05T17:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 5,
                                1921—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 5—2:45
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>80. My 64, January 20 [<hi rendition="#italic">27</hi>], 7 p.m.<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d376-f1"/> British Minister has informed me formally of instructions
                    received by him to secure annulment of Federal contract. His protest based on
                    articles 6 and 12 of wireless contract forwarded by Legation’s 3118 of December
                    5th, 1918 [<hi rendition="#italic">1919</hi>].<anchor n="10" xml:id="d376-f2"
                    /></p>
                <p>Danish protest now on ground cable contract.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d376-f3"/></p>
                <p>I fear the present vehement British and Japanese pressure on present weak Cabinet
                    here will be successful although individually all members, especially Minister
                    of Foreign Affairs and Minister of Communications, recognize great desirability
                    of establishing this means of open and cheap communication between the two
                    peoples.</p>
                <p>I suggest matter be arranged between the Department and the Governments concerned
                    and I ask for instructions. Moss now in the United States.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
